## Target API Functions

1. `cbor_value_is_boolean`
​ `cbor_value_is_boolean()` is a simple type check helper. Use it on a `CborValue*` to test whether the current item is a CBOR boolean. It returns `true` only when `value->type == CborBooleanType`, otherwise `false`.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
/* Booleans */
CBOR_INLINE_API bool cbor_value_is_boolean(const CborValue *value);
​ ```
2. `cbor_value_is_byte_string`
​ Checks whether a `CborValue` currently points to a CBOR byte string. Use it to type-test before reading/extracting bytes. It returns true only when `value->type == CborByteStringType`; otherwise false.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
/* Strings */
CBOR_INLINE_API bool cbor_value_is_byte_string(const CborValue *value);
​ ```
3. `cbor_value_is_text_string`
​ Checks whether a `CborValue` currently points to a CBOR text string. Use it on a valid, initialized `CborValue` to test the item type before reading as text. Returns `true` only when `value->type == CborTextStringType`, otherwise `false`.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
CBOR_INLINE_API bool cbor_value_is_text_string(const CborValue *value);
​ ```
4. `cbor_value_string_iteration_at_end`
​ Checks whether a string iterator has reached the last chunk. Use it during incremental string iteration on a `CborValue`. It returns true only when `cbor_value_get_string_chunk_size()` reports `CborErrorNoMoreStringChunks`; otherwise false.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
CBOR_INLINE_API bool cbor_value_string_iteration_at_end(const CborValue *value);
​ ```
5. `cbor_value_get_text_string_chunk`
​ Returns the next chunk of a text string. Use only when `cbor_value_is_text_string(value)` is true. It fills `bufferptr`/`len` with the chunk and `next` with the following `CborValue`; it delegates to `_cbor_value_get_string_chunk` and asserts on non-text values.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
CBOR_INLINE_API CborError cbor_value_get_text_string_chunk(const CborValue *value, const char **bufferptr,
 size_t *len, CborValue *next);
​ ```
6. `cbor_value_is_null`
​ `cbor_value_is_null` is a simple type check for a `CborValue`. Use it to test whether the value currently points to CBOR `null`. It returns `true` only when `value->type == CborNullType`; otherwise `false`.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
/* Null & undefined type */
CBOR_INLINE_API bool cbor_value_is_null(const CborValue *value);
​ ```

