​ ```
2. `cbor_value_get_string_length`
​ Returns the length of a definite CBOR byte/text string. Use only after checking the value is a string; it asserts on non-strings. If length is unknown, returns `CborErrorUnknownLength`. If the stored length won’t fit in `size_t`, returns `CborErrorDataTooLarge`.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
CBOR_INLINE_API CborError cbor_value_get_string_length(const CborValue *value, size_t *length);
​ ```
3. `cbor_value_dup_byte_string`
​ Duplicates a CBOR byte string into a newly allocated `uint8_t*`. Use it only on byte-string values; it asserts otherwise. `buffer` gets the copy, `buflen` its length, and `next` can receive the following CBOR item. It delegates to the generic string duplicator.
